<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghiyath al-Din Tughluq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned 1320–1325</span> · Also known as Ghazi Malik</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ghiyath al-Din Tughluq, earlier known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a> Malik, was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> from 1320 to 1325 and founder of the Tughluq dynasty. A frontier commander who had fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, he seized power after the fall of the Khalji dynasty and built the fortress city of Tughlaqabad. His armies campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirhut">Tirhut</a>, and he died in 1325 when a pavilion collapsed on him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ghiyath-al-din-tughluq.jpg" alt="Ghiyath al-Din Tughluq" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1410 painter and writer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shah_Ghiyath_al-Din_Tughluq_arrives_in_Tirhut._Depicted_by_eyewitness_Muhammad_Sadr_Ala-i_in_his_BasaUn_al-uns,_ca.1410._Istanbul,_Topkapi_Palace_Museum_Library,_Ms._R.1032_(the_Shah).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
